      "level": 1,
      "topic": "football",
      "title_zh": "门口的男生",
      "title_en": "The boy by my door",
      "paragraphs": [
        ["我", "家", "门口", "有", "一", "个", "小", "地方", "，", "我", "常常", "在", "那里", "玩", "球", "。"],
        ["今天", "，", "一", "个", "男生", "也", "来", "了", "。", "他", "十", "岁", "。", "他", "问", "我", "：", "“", "我", "能", "跟", "你", "一起", "玩", "吗", "？", "”"],
        ["我", "说", "：", "“", "好", "！", "”", "他", "跑", "起来", "很", "快", "，", "进", "了", "三", "个", "球", "。", "我", "一", "个", "也", "没", "进", "。"],
        ["他", "笑", "着", "说", "：", "“", "我", "也", "喜欢", "曼联", "！", "明天", "再", "来", "！", "”"],
        ["我", "想", "，", "明天", "我", "要", "认真", "一", "点", "。"]
      ],
      "translations": [
        "There's a little space outside my front door where I often play football.",
        "Today a boy came along too. He's ten. He asked me: “Can I play with you?”",
        "I said: “Sure!” He was really fast and scored three goals. I didn't score a single one.",
        "He smiled and said: “I like Man United too! I’ll come again tomorrow!”",
        "I think tomorrow I need to try a bit harder."
      ],
      "names": ["曼联"],
      "new_words": ["门口", "常常", "男生"],
      "glossary": [
        { "word": "门口", "english": "doorway; entrance" },
        { "word": "常常", "english": "often" },
        { "word": "男生", "english": "boy" },
        { "word": "曼联", "english": "Manchester United" }
      ]
    },
